\section{The decision indicator}{

The boundary a trial ended at is data, and it reaches the density as
an addition term:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{frm(bf(rt | dec(response) ~ condition), family = wiener(), data = dat)
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

\code{dec()} is spelled as brms spells it and takes what brms takes: a
factor or character vector whose SECOND level is the upper boundary
(so \code{"lower"}/\code{"upper"} and \code{c(FALSE, TRUE)} both work as they read),
or a numeric 0/1 column. The package contributes the term to frmtmb's
addition-term registry when it loads.

\code{vint()} also still works, and carries the indicator as a plain 0/1
integer column:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{frm(bf(rt | vint(upper) ~ condition), family = wiener(), data = dat)
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

Supplying neither is refused with a message that says so, because the
